      "title": "Why side quests get in the way",
      "minutes": 3,
      "html": "      <p>While a pair works on the main thing, small things come up: a flaky test, a flag to rename, a doc to fix. Each is ten minutes of work.</p>\n      <p>Handing them to the coder breaks its focus and muddies the PM&#x27;s review. Doing them yourself in the coder&#x27;s checkout is worse: you&#x27;ll switch a branch under it, or commit its half-finished change.</p>\n      <p>So they get their own task and their own agent, and they stay out of the pair&#x27;s way.</p>"
